<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <%- include('../partials/head') %>
        <title>Drowsy Vocals Privacy Notice</title>
    </head>
    <body>
        <main class="privacy-page">
            <header class="privacy-heading">
                <p class="privacy-eyebrow">Drowsy Vocals</p>
                <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
                <p>This notice explains how Drowsy Vocals handles personal information when you use the management portal and related community services.</p>
                <a href="/">Return to Drowsy Vocals</a>
            </header>

            <article class="privacy-document">
                <section>
                    <h2>Who operates the service</h2>
                    <p>Drowsy Vocals is operated from the United Kingdom. For privacy questions or requests, contact <a href="mailto:support@drowsyvocals.com">support@drowsyvocals.com</a>. The production application and MongoDB database are hosted on self-managed Hostinger infrastructure in Manchester, UK.</p>
                    <p>People may use the service from the UK, the EU, the US, Canada, and other locations. Privacy rights and requirements can differ depending on where you live.</p>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h2>Information we handle</h2>
                    <p>Depending on how you use the service, we may handle:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Discord identifiers, usernames, profile images, account roles, house membership, and account preferences.</li>
                        <li>Login credentials in hashed form, session data, login times, and login IP addresses used for account security.</li>
                        <li>Staff applications, including age information and written answers; staff activity, attendance, voice-session, event, and house-point records.</li>
                        <li>Moderation, leave, appeal, check-in, feedback, and audit records, including details submitted to explain or resolve a case.</li>
                        <li>Images and files you upload, such as profile images, profile backgrounds, and check-in attachments.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Please do not submit passwords or information that is not needed for your request or application.</p>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h2>Why we use it</h2>
                    <p>We use this information to operate accounts and staff applications, manage community membership and activities, provide moderation and support, maintain security, communicate service-related updates, and keep operational records. The legal basis for each use depends on the applicable law and needs a separate review; this notice does not certify that legal assessment.</p>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h2>Services that may receive information</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Hostinger:</strong> hosts the application and its database in Manchester, UK.</li>
                        <li><strong>Discord:</strong> is used for community accounts and, where enabled, staff messages and notifications.</li>
                        <li><strong>Google:</strong> Google Forms may collect application responses before sending them to this service. The site also loads Material Symbols fonts from Google Fonts; that connection can disclose technical browser information, including your IP address, to Google.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Discord and Google may process information in other countries under their own services and terms. The transfer arrangements applicable to each integration should be confirmed with the operator; this notice does not certify a particular transfer mechanism.</p>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
                    <p>The portal uses an essential sign-in session cookie, which expires after 24 hours. It is HTTP-only, uses SameSite=Lax, and is marked Secure in production. The site does not currently use analytics or advertising cookies. A theme preference is stored in your browser's local storage.</p>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h2>Retention</h2>
                    <p>The application currently applies these automated cleanup periods:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Denied applications are removed after 6 months.</li>
                        <li>Voice-session records, attendance, audit and house-point logs, notifications, and deleted-account history are cleaned up after 12 months.</li>
                        <li>Completed check-ins and resolved appeals and support feedback are removed after 12 months. Event feedback is removed after 12 months. Open check-ins and unresolved cases are retained while they remain open.</li>
                        <li>The last-login IP address is cleared 90 days after the associated login, unless a later login replaces it.</li>
                        <li>Closed privacy requests are retained for 12 months.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Automated cleanup does not yet cover every record type; accepted application records and some other operational records may be kept while needed to administer the service. Deleting a live record does not immediately remove copies in backups. Backup rotation is controlled separately by the hosting configuration; a 90-day target has not yet been verified.</p>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h2>Your choices and privacy requests</h2>
                    <p>Depending on where you live, you may be able to request access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability, or object to certain uses of your personal information. Sign in and use <a href="/privacy-requests">Privacy &amp; Data Requests</a>, or email <a href="mailto:support@drowsyvocals.com">support@drowsyvocals.com</a> if you cannot sign in. We may need to verify your identity before acting. Requests are reviewed by staff; submitting a form does not itself delete records.</p>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h2>Age requirement</h2>
                    <p>You must be at least 13 years old to submit an application or use application routes, including submissions received through external forms. If you believe a person under 13 has submitted information, contact us so we can review and remove it where appropriate. This age rule does not by itself establish that the service is suitable for every child or satisfy every child-privacy law.</p>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h2>Security and changes</h2>
                    <p>We use account controls and technical safeguards intended to protect information, but no online service can guarantee absolute security. We may update this notice as the service changes. For questions about privacy practices, contact <a href="mailto:support@drowsyvocals.com">support@drowsyvocals.com</a>.</p>
                </section>
            </article>
            <div class="footer"><p>&copy; 2026 Drowsy Vocals | All rights reserved.</p></div>
        </main>
    </body>
</html>
